	(text "J501-J503: HOYS harness headers (D021/D024) - Vcc / GND / Vout / Vref / OCD, pin-for-pin with the transducer signal pins.\nU501-U503 are busbar-mounted off-board (exclude_from_board); the headers carry their nets on the PCB.\nPart: JST PA B05B-PASK-1 (5-pin, 2.00 mm, vertical, with boss; 3 A, 250 V; mates PAP-05V-S + SPH-002T-P0.5).\nFOOTPRINT CORRECTED: the value said JST PA but the footprint was JST PH B5B-PH-K. PA and PH are NOT intermateable -\nsame 2.00 mm pitch, but different housings (PA 12.0 x 5.3 mm with a 1.1 mm locating boss vs PH 11.7 x 4.5 mm, no boss),\ndifferent latch, different mating families (PAP-**V-S vs PHR-n) and different wire range. There is no JST PA footprint\nin the official KiCad libraries, so mcuc:JST_PA_B05B-PASK-1_1x05_P2.00mm_Vertical was created from the JST ePA-F drawing:\n5 x 0.75 mm plated holes on 2.00 mm pitch (8.00 mm span), 1.1 mm non-plated boss hole 1.5 mm beyond pin 1 and 1.7 mm off\nthe pin-row centreline, 12.0 x 5.3 mm body outline (2.2 mm behind / 3.1 mm in front of the pin row).\n\nREVERSAL HAZARD: the PA housing is keyed and latched, but an unkeyed or hand-made harness plugged in reversed connects\npin 1 (+3.3 V) to pin 5 (OCD) and pin 2 (GND) to pin 4 (Uref). OCD is an open-drain pin on OC_TRIP, so +3.3 V on it does\nnot damage anything (it is already the pull-up rail) but it defeats the wire-OR for that phase; Uref driven to GND puts\nthe servo output at 0 V and forces a permanent trip, which is the safe direction. Build/assembly rule: the harness must\nuse the JST PA housing (PAP-05V-S) so the boss and latch enforce orientation - do not substitute a PH shell."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 165.1 240.03 0)
