	(text "LEM HOYS 200-S/SP33 (U501-U503), datasheet 21Oct2021/v6:
  Pinout (p.15): 1 = UC +3.3 V, 2 = GND, 3 = Uout, 4 = Uref (IN/OUT), 5 = OCD (open drain, active low).
  Sensitivity 2.3 mV/A; Uref 1.63 / 1.65 / 1.67 V behind an internal Rref 130-300R (overdrivable
  0.5-1.7 V); Rout 2-5R; range +/-500 A; BW 180 kHz (p.6).
  Primary = busbar through the aperture: IP+ -> IP- is PHASE_x -> PHASE_x_OUT; Uout > Uref for
  positive IP in the arrow direction (p.15).
  Cref 1 uF / CUC 47 nF in the connection figure are INTERNAL (p.15); the 100 nF per device is
  fitted anyway as local supply decoupling at the board-side connector.

Uref is NOT bused: each Uref pin is a driven output (and an overdrive input, p.6/p.13). Paralleling
three would fight the internal references through their 130-300R series resistances - hence
individual HOYS_x_REF / I_REF_1..3 per phase.

THE TRANSDUCER IS NOT RATIOMETRIC (review 3 MJ-4). The previous note here claimed the thresholds
were 'ratiometric to the same 3.3 V rail' - that was FALSE. Uref and the 2.3 mV/A sensitivity are
ABSOLUTE, set inside the device; they do not track +3.3 V. A threshold divider hung off +3.3 V
smeared the 300 A trip over 245-356 A (+/-4 % rail against a fixed transducer reference, plus the
+/-20 mV Uref spread)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 204 100 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "22192241-1d31-4ce2-95a9-9e2fbd8755eb")
	)
	(text "300 A hardware trip (SPEC 9.1): 300 A x 2.3 mV/A = 690 mV about that phase's OWN Uref
-> 2.34 V / 0.96 V at Uref = 1.65 V.
Thresholds are now servo-derived from that phase's Uref (U507-U509 = OPA376AIDBVR, Vos 25 uV max,
RRIO, 2.2-5.5 V, 5.5 MHz, $2.15, 5962 stk):
  op-amp out = V_HI -[R502 6.19k]- FB tap -[R503 6.19k]- V_LO -[R504 8.62k]- GND,
  FB tap returned to the (-) input. The loop forces FB = Uref, so
  V_HI = Uref x 21.00/14.81 = 1.41796 x Uref = 2.3396 V, V_LO = V_HI x 8.62/21.00 = 0.9604 V.
  Trip half-window = 0.41796 x Uref = 689.6 mV -> 299.8 A, and it TRACKS Uref, not the rail.
  Errors: Uref 1.63-1.67 V -> +/-3.6 A; string 0.1 % -> +/-0.6 A; TLV7022 Vos +/-8 mV max ->
  +/-3.5 A; op-amp Vos negligible. Worst case ~ +/-8 A about 300 A (was 245-356 A).
  String current 2.34 V / 21.0k = 111 uA; V_HI 2.34 V is inside the OPA376's rail-to-rail output.

Window comparator (open-drain: OUT = LOW when V- > V+), all six outputs wire-OR'd on OC_TRIP:
  A (upper): V+ = V_HI,  V- = Vout  ->  LOW when Vout > V_HI  (I > +300 A)
  B (lower): V+ = Vout,  V- = V_LO  ->  LOW when Vout < V_LO  (I < -300 A)
  |I| < 300 A: both Hi-Z -> OC_TRIP held HIGH by R907 4.7k (supervisor sheet). Either polarity
  pulls OC_TRIP LOW -> U901D (NAND as inverter, pin 13) clocks the 74AUP1G74 fault latch.
  This restores the PALTA active-low wired-OR ~OC_Fault structure (D018/D019)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 204 172 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b620a678-6783-4ace-b648-b6c191ca132b")
	)
	(text "COMPARATOR = TI TLV7022DDFR (SLVSDM5F), dual, TRUE OPEN-DRAIN, rail-to-rail input (VEE to
VCC+0.1 V), 1.6-6.5 V, tPLH 260 ns / tPHL 310 ns typ, sink 33 mA, DDF = SOT-23-8 thin.
Corrects review 3 MJ-2/MJ-3, where the fitted part was wrong twice over: TLV7032 is PUSH-PULL
(six push-pull outputs wire-OR'd against three open-drain OCD pins = direct output contention),
and LM2903's input common-mode range on 3.3 V is 0-1.8 V, BELOW the 2.34 V upper threshold - the
over-current half could never trip. Both were also ~3 us parts against SPEC 9.1's < 1 us.
TLV702x/704x are NOT offered in SOIC-8, so the old SOIC-8 footprint was unbuildable.
No external hysteresis: the outputs are wire-OR'd onto a latched line, so chatter cannot un-trip,
and per-comparator feedback would couple all three phase thresholds through the shared net.
TLV7022's own hysteresis is 7.2 mV typ / 15 mV max (up to 6.5 A, one-sided - it only tightens).

FAIL-SAFE HARNESS BIAS (review 3 MJ-7): R514/R518/R522 100k pull HOYS_x_OUT down to GND and
R515/R519/R523 1M pull HOYS_x_REF up to +3.3 V. An unplugged J50x now reads a large negative
current and latches the trip at power-up before HV is applied, instead of silently dropping that
phase's OCD out of the wire-OR and floating the ADC/comparator input.
Loading error: 1.65 V / 100k = 16.5 uA into Rout 2-5R = 33-83 uV = 0.014-0.036 A (< 0.04 A). The
1M on Uref injects 1.65 uA into Rref 130-300R = 0.21-0.50 mV = 0.09-0.22 A of offset - both far
inside the transducer's own +/-1.25 % at 25 C. EEPROM-error forces Uout to GND (p.5 note 1) ->
also caught by the lower comparator."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 204 232 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "526c62eb-efd2-4ebc-86c8-2b32074ed113")
	)
	(text "Transducer OCD pins (open drain, active low, 2.92 x Ipn ~ 584 A pk +/-10%, p.6) stay wire-OR'd
onto OC_TRIP as an independent backup trip; the DS p.15 pull-up 'R' to UC is the shared R907.

RC anti-alias 100R + 1 nF on each I_PH_x AND now on each I_REF_x (R513/R517/R521 + C510/C512/C514,
review 3 MN-9), so the differential read Uout - Uref sees matched delays and the common mode
cancels; fc ~ 1.6 MHz, Rout 2-5R, CL max 6 nF. The servo taps I_REF_x downstream of its RC,
matching the comparator's tap downstream of the I_PH_x RC.

C516 1 nF at the board end of OC_TRIP (review 3 MN-8): 450 pC of injected charge now moves the
node 0.45 V instead of latching the bridge off. Assert-edge cost: the open-drain sinks >= 5 mA, so
1 nF crosses the receiver threshold in ~330 ns; with tPHL 310 ns the comparator-to-latch path is
~0.65 us, still inside SPEC 9.1's < 1 us. Release is R907 x C516 = 4.7 us.
A Schmitt-trigger receiver at the supervisor end is still wanted - that pin is on the supervisor
sheet and is NOT changed here."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 196 285 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9134abd1-4601-4faa-ab6d-7a4e985efec3")
	)
	(text "MOTOR PHASE OUTPUT TERMINALS J406-J408 (review 3 MJ-7 / MN-20).
PHASE_U/V/W_OUT were SINGLE-NODE nets - the only thing on each was the HOYS primary IP- pin, and
there was no motor phase terminal anywhere in the design even though D021 states the phase busbars
pass through the transducer apertures to M6 output studs. The three studs are now captured.
Convention follows J401-J405 (D024): a Screw_Terminal_01x01 symbol carrying a ring-lug pad
footprint, here MountingHole:MountingHole_6.4mm_M6_Pad_Via. Marked exclude_from_board (on_board no)
because the studs are on the busbar assembly, not on the control PCB - power current never flows
through this board (D021). They exist so netlist, BOM and ERC all see a terminated phase output.
ROOT SHEET: the PHASE_U/V/W_OUT hierarchical labels still drive root sheet pins that go nowhere.
Delete those three root sheet pins (the net is now fully local to this sheet) - see the report."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 215.9 58 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "404ec16c-7ca5-472e-838f-0b9ace5eeb03")
	)

